        "faq_item_XJKL8m": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which Kestrel knife should I choose?",
            "answer": "It really comes down to what you want the knife to do.\nThe Ovis Hunter is our do-it-all hunting knife and the knife I recommend if you want one blade capable of handling most of the work on an animal.\nThe Mouflon Skinner is more specialized toward skinning and processing. \nThe Mountain Caper is built for detailed caping and precision work. \nThe Ovis Scalpel gives you the convenience of replaceable blades and comfort like no other scalpel on the market.\nIf weight is your biggest concern, The Mountain Scalpel or our Skeleton models give you the performance of a fixed blade without the additional weight of traditional handles.\nStill not sure? Email us at sales@kestrelknives.com. Tell us what and how you hunt and we'll point you in the right direction",
            "category": "Featured Questions",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_T9xUkQ": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between the Ovis Hunter and Mouflon Skinner?",
            "answer": "The biggest difference is blade geometry and what each knife was designed to do.\nThe Ovis Hunter is our all-purpose hunting knife. Its slight trailing-point design and upswept tip give you plenty of belly for skinning and long slicing cuts while still maintaining a fine point for detailed work. It's designed to move from one job to the next without needing to switch knives.\nThe Mouflon Skinner is more specialized. Its geometry is built around skinning and gives you a purpose-built cutting surface for separating hide and working through an animal efficiently.\nIf you want one knife to do a little bit of everything, go with the Ovis Hunter. If you want a dedicated skinner, that's where the Mouflon shines.",
            "category": "Featured Questions",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_MfN4qJ": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why does Kestrel use MagnaCut?",
            "answer": "Because hunting knives need more than a steel that just holds an edge.\nWe need a steel that can stay sharp while processing an animal, resist corrosion from blood and moisture, and still have the toughness required for real field use.\nCPM MagnaCut gives us an exceptional balance of edge retention, toughness and corrosion resistance. That's why you'll see it across many of our hunting knives.",
            "category": "Featured Questions",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_MmtgPh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do Kestrel Knives come with free lifetime sharpening?",
            "answer": "Yes! Our fixed-blade knives include free lifetime sharpening for customers in the continental United States.\nYou ship the knife to us. We'll put a fresh edge on it, clean it up and ship it back to you free of charge.\nThese knives are meant to be used. Don't be afraid to use yours.",
            "category": "Featured Questions",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_BmwNA3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you rewrap paracord handles?",
            "answer": "Yes. Paracord rewraps are free.\nIf you're sending your knife in for sharpening, just put a note in the package telling us you'd like the paracord replaced.\nIf that old wrap has been on a few hunts and you'd rather keep it, we'll leave it alone and can include a fresh piece of paracord for when you're ready to change it.",
            "category": "Featured Questions",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_DK7F8A": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does the Kestrel Knives Lifetime Warranty cover?",
            "answer": "Our Lifetime Warranty covers manufacturing defects in materials and workmanship for the functional life of the knife.\nIf we determine your knife has a manufacturing defect, we'll repair or replace it at no charge at our discretion.\nIt doesn't cover misuse, abuse, prying, batoning, improper sharpening, unauthorized modifications, neglect, corrosion or damage caused by using the knife outside its intended purpose. Normal scratches and finish wear aren't defects either. They're usually just signs that you're actually using your knife.\nIf something happens, contact us. Photos help, but we may need to physically inspect the knife before determining what happened and what we can do.",
            "category": "Featured Questions",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_EGtMd7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is CPM MagnaCut?",
            "answer": "CPM MagnaCut is a premium American-made stainless knife steel developed specifically for cutlery.\nWhat makes it impressive isn't one individual property. It's the balance of edge retention, toughness and corrosion resistance.\nFor a hunting knife that can be exposed to blood, moisture, dirt and hard use, that's exactly the kind of balance we're after.",
            "category": "Knives & Steel",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_ycFC8t": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between the Ovis Hunter and Mouflon Skinner?",
            "answer": "The biggest difference is blade geometry.\nThe Ovis Hunter is designed to be a do-it-all hunting knife. Its slight trailing-point design gives you an upswept tip, plenty of belly and a fine point. That makes it useful for everything from long skinning cuts to more controlled detail work.\nThe Mouflon Skinner is more specialized toward skinning and processing.\nIf you're looking for one knife to cover a wide range of jobs, I'd look at the Ovis Hunter. If you already know you want a dedicated skinner, look at the Mouflon.",
            "category": "Knives & Steel",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_JjgkV7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why does Kestrel use MagnaCut?",
            "answer": "We don't pick steel because the name looks good on a product page.\nFor hunting knives, we want edge retention, toughness and corrosion resistance. Improving one of those properties often comes at the expense of another.\nMagnaCut gives us an excellent balance of all three, which makes it a great fit for the type of knives we build.",
            "category": "Knives & Steel",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_PWKfTh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does MagnaCut compare to Nitro-V?",
            "answer": "Nitro-V is a very capable stainless knife steel. It's tough, corrosion resistant and relatively easy to sharpen.\nMagnaCut takes things further, particularly when you're looking at the overall combination of edge retention, toughness and corrosion resistance.\nThere's nothing wrong with Nitro-V. We simply believe MagnaCut's balance of properties makes it a better fit for many of our hunting knives.",
            "category": "Knives & Steel",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_wVXHqE": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does MagnaCut compare to S35VN?",
            "answer": "S35VN is a proven premium knife steel and has been used successfully in quality knives for years.\nMagnaCut was developed more recently with a major focus on balancing toughness, edge retention and corrosion resistance.\nBoth are good steels. For the wet, dirty and sometimes rough conditions hunting knives see, we prefer the overall balance MagnaCut gives us.",
            "category": "Knives & Steel",
            "show_item": true
          }
        },
        "faq_item_DnjTqF": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does MagnaCut rust?",
            "answer": "MagnaCut is extremely corrosion resistant, but that doesn't mean you should throw a bloody knife into a wet sheath and forget about it.\nClean the blade after processing an animal, dry it thoroughly and don't store it wet or dirty.\nTake care of your knife and it'll take care of you.",
            "category": "Knives & Steel",
            "show_item": true
          }
        }
